The design of the optional Jev decision loop was informed by the MIT-licensed
projects jev-browser-use (wy-coliney) and jev-desktop (yikangy873-gif). This
plugin is an independent Windows-first implementation with a local deterministic
mode, narrowed data boundary, confirmation handoffs, and its own runtime/tests.

Long-page screenshot composition uses jpeg-js (BSD-3-Clause) and pngjs (MIT).
Their license files are included in node_modules after npm ci; dependency source
and runtime artifacts are not included in this source repository.

Upstream project references (design inspiration, not bundled applications):
https://github.com/wy-coliney/jev-browser-use (MIT)
https://github.com/yikangy873-gif/jev-desktop (MIT)

Dependency sources and licenses:
https://github.com/jpeg-js/jpeg-js (BSD-3-Clause)
https://github.com/pngjs/pngjs (MIT)

